  "body": "Slice 1 of #220: an engagement-controlled trochoid generator and a standalone **Trochoidal slot** operation. Branched from upstream/main; the fork is synced at v0.15.0.\n\n## What changed\n**The generator** (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/trochoid_slot.rs`, `trochoid_loops.rs`, `trochoid_air.rs`), specced from Otkur & Lazoglu 2007 and Rauch, Duc & Hascoet 2009.\n- **Loop shape:** each loop is the front arc of a circle of radius ρ = B / cos 10°, with B = (W − D)/2 by default. The arc runs wall to wall and meets each wall at 10°.\n  - On a straight chain the loops are shifted copies, so they never cross. Classic full-circle trochoids always cross the previous loop, and the verifier holds the post on a same-depth crossing.\n  - A wall move between arcs cleans the cusp, and a fillet (the smoothing radius) blends it into each arc.\n- **Start and end:** a helical bore of radius B at the start. A stepped fan of arcs closes the far end.\n- **Returns:** microlift (default 0.3 mm, retracing the arc just cut at the return feed) or retract.\n- **Engagement:** measured with the Adaptive pins' dexel yardstick (`quality::measure`) on each candidate level. The planner tries steps from 100% of the user's step down to 7%, and a note says when the step was cut. Adaptive's planner raster was not reused because it counts finished walls as contact (see the decision file).\n- **Lifted returns over air:** a new `machining2d::lifted_cut` checks each lifted return against the in-process stock.\n- **Refused by name:**\n  - a channel narrower than the tool (it suggests a plain Slot);\n  - a loop wider than the room;\n  - a limit no step can hold (the message gives the lowest reading, where it was, and at which step);\n  - a loop leaving the channel;\n  - a crossing (the verifier's own `crossed_pairs`);\n  - a lifted return over stock.\n\n**The operation:** `OpType::TrochoidalSlot` (kind 39) in the ribbon's 2D mill family.\n- **Authoring:** two endpoints and a width, like Slot, verified against the slot's stadium.\n- **Parameters:** loop width (auto), forward step, max engagement, return, microlift height, smoothing radius, stock to leave, heights, stepdown, cutting/return/plunge feeds, climb.\n- **Undo and editing:** create and edit are undoable (`CreateOperation` / `EditOperationParams`). It has a small Geometry/Heights/Passes/Feeds page.\n- **Project file:** a `trochoidal_slot` params entry. There is no `PROJECT_VERSION` bump, following the probe op's precedent (#108/#344) for an appended kind. Older builds won't read a document that uses the new kind.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/220-trochoidal-slot.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- **motion `trochoid_slot`** (7 tests, plus 2 unit tests):\n  - A full-width slot (D10 in W16, 1 mm step) measures θmax **66.5°**; a straight Slot in the same channel measures **180°**.\n  - A 60° limit forces the step down, and the note says so.\n  - The verifier is clean (no crossing, gouge or rapid-in-stock) for climb and conventional, microlift and retract.\n  - Microlift returns land on air, and the check catches one placed over stock.\n  - Named refusals; the loops post as arcs.\n- **app `trochoid_op`:** create and edit undo/redo; generate verifies clean and posts G03; a too-narrow channel is refused by name; project round trip.\n- **New goldens:** `golden/trochoid_slot_small.cl` and `golden/nc/trochoid_slot_small.nc` (Fanuc, G02/G03).\n- **Edited tests:** `ribbon` and `probe_op` pinned the probe as the last kind; they now pin index 38, and kind 39 is pinned.\n- **Passing:**\n  - motion `adaptive_band`;\n  - app mill2d_b/c, ribbon, tool_law, probe_op, golden_cl, fanuc_post, project_roundtrip, operations, commands_undo, conformance, heidenhain_block_form, slot_caps, drill_prior_kinds, pick_doors, setup_align, wall_column_gouge, drilling_axial;\n  - ui kind/ribbon/tab tests (including `every_registry_kind_gets_its_tab_bar`) and ui `operations`;\n  - clippy on motion, app and ui (`-D warnings`).\n- **Runtime:** the `trochoid_slot` binary takes about 80 s in debug when run in parallel. Each test is under 25 s alone.\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\n- **No run yet:** a GUI hands-on check, and a Hub or machine run of the posted arcs. This adds new posted G-code.\n- **Deferred to later slices:** Adaptive's trochoidal mode (Done means 2), the corner-overload pin, centre-line picking from a model chain (typed endpoints today), the in-plane cutting return, feed reduction where engagement rises, and wall finishing when the loop band is narrower than the room.\n\nChangelog: Trochoidal slot operation: an engagement-controlled trochoid along a typed centre line - measured contact angle held under a limit by adapting the step, microlift or retract returns, named refusals (#220, slice 1)\n\nRefs #220\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
